DPM benchmark runtime=LuaJIT 2.1 via OBS lua51.dll; seed=268; frames=60 at 60 Hz
Timer: LuaJIT FFI QueryPerformanceCounter; module/fixture/HUD setup is untimed.
Each fresh sample fixture runs one untimed workload callsite warm-up, then resets state and counters before the timed workload.
Each case also discards two complete sample runs per variant before measurement; warm-up pair order is AB then BA, so both variants receive two warm-ups.
Measured samples are paired by identical inputs; pair order alternates AB/BA. Every case has at least 12 pairs; 200 units/500 events has 24.
GC condition: memory baseline follows two full collections; GC stopped from fixture creation through internal warm-up, measurement, and cleanup; full collection after each sample.
CSV rows preserve every measured variant run and all operation counters. Summary includes avg/min/median/max and paired after-minus-baseline elapsed differences.
elapsed_ms is observational only with no pass/fail threshold. GameSession field reads count mocked game_object_field calls, not engine telemetry.
memory_delta_kb spans fixture/module setup, internal warm-up, hot workload, and cleanup until before collection; it is not retained live-mod memory.
